Accumulation of Pb in soil and various plant parts

The findings in Table 4 demonstrate that SeNPs and BP-BC application, whether separately or in conjunction,
markedly diminished Pb buildup in soil, shoots, roots, and seeds. Significantly, BP-BC sole addition was more
efficacious in reducing Pb concentrations in both plant tissues and soil than the SeNPs application. Specifically,
application of BP-BC at 5 t ha−1 and 10 t ha−1 led to reductions in Pb accumulation in the following ways:
